WEBVTT

00:00:04.152 --> 00:00:05.112
(WHIRRING)

00:00:05.192 --> 00:00:06.272
(PANTING)

00:00:06.352 --> 00:00:07.392
CAR 1: That was amazing.
CAR 2: Awesome. Yeah!

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:10.192
It's just like being on a real track,
so put your hours in.

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:13.672
Okay, let's hit the treadmills.
Come on. Show me what you got!

00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:16.192
Wow. Pretty fast. Who's the racer?

00:00:16.272 --> 00:00:18.872
No. She's not a racer. She's a trainer.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:22.272
Cruz Ramirez.
The best trainer in the business.

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:24.432
ALL: Ready to meet it,
greet it and defeat it?

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:27.472
All right. Now bring up those RPMs!

00:00:27.592 --> 00:00:29.352
(CHUCKLES) Like the attitude.

00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:31.872
Yeah, we call her
our maestro of motivation.

00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:33.872
You're driving
a little tense again, Ronald.

00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:37.592
-No, no. I'm cool. I'm cool.
-Do your exercise.

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:41.072
I am a fluffy cloud! I am a fluffy cloud!

00:00:41.152 --> 00:00:43.552
I am a fluffy cloud. (SIGHS)

00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:44.832
CRUZ: There you go!

00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:46.792
-You're a cloud. (LAUGHS)
-Shut up, Kurt!

00:00:46.992 --> 00:00:49.872
-Here come the bugs, Kurt. You ready?
-(INHALES SHARPLY)

00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:51.552
(INSECTS BUZZING)

00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:54.232
Hey, I kept my eyes open this time!

00:00:54.552 --> 00:00:55.752
Got to see that track.

00:00:55.832 --> 00:00:58.352
Oh, no. Homesick again, Gabriel?

00:00:58.392 --> 00:00:59.472
Si.

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:02.032
(SPANISH MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:02.872 --> 00:01:05.072
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

00:01:05.312 --> 00:01:07.232
-Win for them!
-McQUEEN: Wow.

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:09.672
STERLING: She trains young racers
to push through their own obstacles.

00:01:09.912 --> 00:01:13.672
Tailor-made for each one.
Now, she's gonna work with you.

00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:16.912
Let's go! Let's go!
You guys got to work through this stuff...

00:01:17.072 --> 00:01:19.032
so when your big chance comes along
you can take it.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.312
Hey, Cruz.

00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:21.912
Oh, hey, Mr. Sterling!

00:01:22.232 --> 00:01:24.672
I'd like to introduce you
to Lightning McQueen.

00:01:24.752 --> 00:01:26.272
I hear you're the maestro.

00:01:26.632 --> 00:01:29.512
Mr. Sterling, did you say
Lightning McQueen was here because...

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:31.432
(SNORTS) I don't see him anywhere.

00:01:31.672 --> 00:01:34.952
Uh, but he's right here.
Do you not see him?

00:01:35.192 --> 00:01:36.392
Nope, still don't see him.

00:01:36.832 --> 00:01:39.912
He's right in front of you!
It's Lightning McQueen!

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:45.072
He's obviously an imposter. He looks old
and broken down with flabby tires.

00:01:45.232 --> 00:01:46.792
-Hey! I do not!
-Use that!

00:01:46.952 --> 00:01:48.712
Whoa! Oh.

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:49.872
Yeah, I see.

00:01:50.032 --> 00:01:52.832
I can use that energy
for motivation, right? (GROWLS)

00:01:53.352 --> 00:01:55.752
It's all about motivation, Mr. McQueen.

00:01:55.912 --> 00:01:59.632
You can use anything negative as fuel
to push through to the positive.

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:02.952
I've been pretty positive
ever since I was a rookie.

00:02:03.192 --> 00:02:05.032
I am so excited that I get to train you.

00:02:05.112 --> 00:02:07.312
I grew up watching you on TV.

00:02:07.672 --> 00:02:09.432
Huh? Is that right?

00:02:09.672 --> 00:02:12.352
These young guys are great and all,
but I like a challenge.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.952
(CHUCKLES)
I'm not that much older, but--

00:02:15.232 --> 00:02:17.792
In fact, I call you my senior project.

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:19.992
(UP-TEMPO MUSIC PLAYING)

00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:23.312
We need to loosen those ancient joints.

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:24.832
First the wheels.

00:02:24.952 --> 00:02:28.552
And forward, and rest,
and forward, and rest.

00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:31.032
Join me! Rest. (HUFFING) And rest.

00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:32.712
Is all this resting necessary?

00:02:32.992 --> 00:02:35.672
We're working you in slowly.
And reach for your lunch.

00:02:36.152 --> 00:02:37.952
Reach for your lunch.

00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:40.752
Now reach, to the front.

00:02:40.912 --> 00:02:44.352
What is there? It's your lunch.

00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:48.152
Now backwards. Is lunch there?

00:02:48.232 --> 00:02:49.472
McQUEEN: When do we go
on the simulator?

00:02:49.952 --> 00:02:52.512
CRUZ: Good morning,
Mr. McQueen. Looking good.

00:02:52.592 --> 00:02:53.672
(YELPS AND GRUNTS)

00:02:54.392 --> 00:02:55.632
Why?

00:02:55.912 --> 00:02:59.672
This'll get oil to places
it hasn't been in a long time.

00:03:00.232 --> 00:03:03.312
-Is that a drip pan?
-Just in case.

00:03:03.472 --> 00:03:04.952
How old do you think I am?

00:03:05.032 --> 00:03:07.992
Visualize yourself driving fast
down a steep hill.

00:03:08.032 --> 00:03:09.272
I'll be back in a few.

00:03:09.672 --> 00:03:13.472
Visualize... Wait. Cruz! A few what?

00:03:13.512 --> 00:03:15.312
I just want to go on the simulator.

00:03:15.352 --> 00:03:17.712
KURT: How's it hanging, Drip Pan?

00:03:18.232 --> 00:03:19.712
(ENGINES ROARING)

00:03:26.032 --> 00:03:28.512
-'Sup?
-Okay, day three...

00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:32.432
Treadmill. I've set a maximum
speed to conserve your energy.

00:03:32.592 --> 00:03:36.192
What I want you to do is
visualize beating this guy.

00:03:36.352 --> 00:03:37.392
(McQUEEN GRUNTS)

00:03:37.552 --> 00:03:39.072
-Storm!
-Uh-huh, that's right.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.472
Get him! Get him, Mr. McQueen!

00:03:40.672 --> 00:03:43.592
Get him? This thing's only
going like 5 miles an hour!

00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:46.512
We'll work up to the higher speeds
right after you take your nap.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:48.632
-Nap? I don't need a nap!
-(RACERS LAUGHING)

00:03:50.352 --> 00:03:51.472
KURT: Hit him with the bugs! (LAUGHS)

00:03:51.992 --> 00:03:53.872
I am not taking a nap!

00:03:54.232 --> 00:03:55.712
ANNOUNCER: All cars in
the test bay simulator--

00:03:55.752 --> 00:03:57.032
(YAWNING)

00:03:57.072 --> 00:03:59.352
How was your nap, Mr. McQueen?

00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:02.192
It was kind of refreshing actually.

00:04:03.152 --> 00:04:04.432
Oh! Okay, what are you-- Hey!

00:04:04.592 --> 00:04:06.712
You've been driving on tires a long time.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.792
Have you ever stopped
to get to know them?

00:04:09.072 --> 00:04:09.992
I'm sorry, what?

00:04:10.152 --> 00:04:13.072
Tires are individuals.
You should give each a name.

00:04:13.392 --> 00:04:16.192
Name them? (SCOFFS)
I won't be doing that.

00:04:16.392 --> 00:04:19.152
Mine are named Maria, Juanita,
Ronaldo, and Debbie Richardson.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.752
-What?
-Long story.

00:04:21.272 --> 00:04:23.272
May I have my tires back so I can go
on the simulator please?

00:04:23.352 --> 00:04:24.232
Name them!

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:27.232
Uh, Lefty, Righty, Backy,
Backy Junior. Okay?

00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:29.072
-Does this make you mad?
-Yes, it does!

00:04:29.312 --> 00:04:32.032
Use that! And merge, and yield,

00:04:32.112 --> 00:04:33.592
-and merge, and yield.
-(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

00:04:33.992 --> 00:04:37.712
Beep, beep, beep, beep.
Now you got some tire damage.

00:04:38.152 --> 00:04:39.272
Speed bump, speed bump.

00:04:39.352 --> 00:04:41.312
Now clean up your messy garage.

00:04:41.512 --> 00:04:46.432
-Bug in your windshield.
-Thank you, Cruz, I'm done.

00:04:47.672 --> 00:04:49.352
Mr. McQueen, where are you going?

00:04:49.512 --> 00:04:50.672
McQUEEN: To the future.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:56.912
Okay. Here we go. How do I do this?

00:04:56.992 --> 00:04:58.512
-Come on, baby.
-Mr. McQueen--

00:04:58.592 --> 00:05:01.352
Cruz, thank you for the old-man
training, as crazy as it was,

00:05:01.432 --> 00:05:04.632
but I'm... warmed up enough
and now I need you to launch this thing.

00:05:04.672 --> 00:05:07.072
Wait until you can handle it. Please?

00:05:07.152 --> 00:05:08.352
-There are no shortcuts.
-(CLICKING)

00:05:08.432 --> 00:05:10.152
Okay. We'll just see about that.

00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:13.232
STERLING: All right.
My star racer is on the simulator!

00:05:13.392 --> 00:05:14.792
Why, yes, I am!

00:05:15.032 --> 00:05:17.112
Well, let's see you
take it out for a spin.

00:05:17.352 --> 00:05:20.952
Right away, Mr. Sterling,
owner of the company.

00:05:23.632 --> 00:05:25.272
Okay. Have fun.

00:05:25.712 --> 00:05:26.752
(CLICKS SWITCH)

00:05:27.032 --> 00:05:28.992
This is what I'm talking about.

00:05:29.072 --> 00:05:30.952
Whoa. Didn't know about those.
(GASPS)

00:05:31.472 --> 00:05:34.992
SIMULATOR: Prepare to race.
The green flag is out.

00:05:35.032 --> 00:05:36.792
I don't see the flag. What do I do?

00:05:36.832 --> 00:05:37.912
-Go.
-Go?

00:05:38.192 --> 00:05:39.432
(REVVING)

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.872
Whoa.

00:05:41.432 --> 00:05:42.952
That's sensitive. (YELPING)

00:05:43.512 --> 00:05:44.792
SIMULATOR: You have hit a wall.

00:05:44.952 --> 00:05:47.392
-It shouldn't be this hard, should it? Ah!
-You have hit a wall.

00:05:47.672 --> 00:05:50.432
You're fighting the simulator.
Just race like you always do.

00:05:51.192 --> 00:05:52.552
-You have hit a wall.
-Whoa.

00:05:52.792 --> 00:05:54.112
There can't be this many walls
on a regular track!

00:05:55.392 --> 00:05:56.992
You have been passed by
Jackson Storm.

00:05:57.352 --> 00:05:59.512
-Wait, Storm's in here?
-For motivation.

00:05:59.752 --> 00:06:02.952
Storm races at 207.
Pick it up, Mr. McQueen!

00:06:03.192 --> 00:06:04.272
I'm trying!

00:06:04.872 --> 00:06:06.232
(GRUNTING)

00:06:08.592 --> 00:06:09.992
-Ahhh!
-You have hit a wall.

00:06:10.152 --> 00:06:12.912
Mr. McQueen, come down from there
and we'll work you up to this.

00:06:13.192 --> 00:06:15.472
I am fine, Cruz. I can do it, okay?

00:06:15.552 --> 00:06:16.552
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:06:17.312 --> 00:06:18.712
-(CRASHING)
-Ahh!

00:06:18.912 --> 00:06:20.392
-You have jumped a barrier.
-Oh!

00:06:20.552 --> 00:06:21.552
(BABBLING)

00:06:22.152 --> 00:06:22.872
(GASPS) Sorry!

00:06:22.952 --> 00:06:24.392
You have maimed two vehicles.

00:06:24.472 --> 00:06:26.352
You have destroyed a drinking fountain.

00:06:26.512 --> 00:06:28.112
(SCREAMING)

00:06:29.752 --> 00:06:31.392
You have disabled an ambulance.

00:06:31.432 --> 00:06:35.032
You are on fire. Danger. Danger.

00:06:35.632 --> 00:06:37.352
You are going the wrong way.

00:06:37.512 --> 00:06:39.232
Look out! Turn it off!

00:06:39.392 --> 00:06:41.352
Get these things off of me!

